  "447": {
    "peri-megadim/part-001.txt": {
      "1:ז":
        "And after consideration I saw that what the Mechaber wrote in Yoreh De'ah 134:2 regarding small barrels being nullified — these are clear matters for halachah; and Pesach is different, for they made several stringencies from what is written: dry in dry is not nullified. And not as the Rashba wrote in Teshuvot HaRosh kvav and in responsum to the Mechaber, and also that we do not follow after the reason. And proof to this from what is written in Pesachim 43a: Rava said the halachah is chametz in its time in its kind and not in its kind in any amount like Rav — it implies certainly that Rav literally holds so; and although not for his reason, nevertheless in the substance of the law he holds like Rav; and now for Rav in its kind in any amount — for Rav also in dry, as Rabbeinu Tam wrote after retraction (see Tosafos Menachot 22 s.v. from here, etc.) (and what we learned that terumah in 101 is nullified in ordinary food that is fixed — see there); and Rav decreed not in its kind lest in its kind — the same applies in dry; Rava also holds thus. And although we have no ruling that the Mechaber would hold thus — in 447:64 and 461 and 453 in Magen Avraham 6: flour in flour is called wet in wet — therefore there is no proof from Beitzah 38b for R' Yehuda that wheat in wheat is not nullified — one may say it deals with flour; and see Tosafos Menachot and Yevamot chapter HaOrlah from this; and seemingly on the contrary there is contradiction to this from what the Mechaber wrote in Tur Choshen Mishpat general 45:6 and in Mechaber Choshen Mishpat 10 who gave a reason for doubt and did not give the Ran's reason brought in Taz Yoreh De'ah 102:5 and his praise because dry in dry in doubt should be nullified. Nevertheless I say the Mechaber from his own reasoning was stringent in chametz since he said in any amount like Rav and holds like Rabbeinu Tam and because of the stringency of chametz; and the halachah is like one view, and as we need to say below it will be explained; and see there he wrote dry in dry is not nullified in its kind specifically of doubt; and it is difficult — for the Rambam even not in its kind holds the reason in chametz because of doubt in chapter 13:13 in Magen Avraham; and Eshel Avraham Yoreh De'ah 102:14 — one may say here that one says dry is nullified in any amount and all hold chametz of doubt, and in its kind not like the Rambam, and not in its kind in wet in any amount because of karet and we do not dismiss; and one may say also the words of Or Sameach are thus; and it will be explained inside.",
    },
  },
  "462": {
    "peri-megadim/part-001.txt": {
      "1:ב":
        "For — in Yoreh De'ah 126:6 — if there is kosher wine in the upper vessel and in the lower vessel, stam yayin is touched: when one pours, the upper remainder is forbidden; and if there is water in it, see as Magen Avraham wrote in letter 2 and Ateret Zekenim letter 2; and in Orach Chayyim 14 there, letter 7, regarding stam yayin of ours there is no need to add water (unless it certainly touched stam yayin); and Eshel Avraham there letter 11: a practical difference in adding water for ours, that it should be nullified in six parts water — see there; and siman 134:65. What Orach Chayyim wrote that se'or and honey disqualify wine — see Yoreh De'ah 123; and Shach letter 8: for ours specifically, if its taste changed it does not forbid in stam yayin — see there.",
    },
  },
